    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 28-layer dielectric coating on fused silica substrate using HfO2 and SiO2 materials. Structure: Air incident | 14 contiguous bilayer units of (HfO2 | SiO2) | Fused Silica. Initialize each bilayer unit with HfO2 thickness = quarter-wave at 1350 nm (geometric mean of 1000-1700 nm band) and SiO2 thickness = quarter-wave at 375 nm (geometric mean of 300-450 nm band), with ±15% random tolerance per layer. Apply soft penalty during optimization to discourage thickness ratio between adjacent layers exceeding 1.4 or falling below 0.714. Optimize all 28 layer thicknesses independently. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Spectral bands: 300-450 nm (maximize reflectance), 1000-1700 nm (maximize transmittance). Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with 500 iterations maximum. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: low transmission in 300-450 nm; low reflection in 1000-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count <= 30; materials restricted to HfO2 and SiO2.",
